      "Note": "The tail's arrowhead tip sways; two small painted flames burn steadily on the two outer prongs' points (the fork is at the tip since 2026-10-29; v3: smaller, slower, a smooth overlapping pulse instead of a blink); a few sparks rise off the fork. No light (a coloured light dyes the body by day)."
    },
    "Aura": {
      "Note": "Opaque painted flames (red, orange only at the tongues' tips) at the two outer arrowheads' points, set back 0.32 from the tip (none on the middle point: it is the cue's tip and meets the ball), and sparks off the fork: no additive mush on the bright floor (coordinator 19:40). v3 (designer 2026-10-29: the two pulsing flames looked choppy): each flame is about 8 overlapping particles locked to the prong's point, each living 1.0-1.25 s (the 16-frame flipbook at about 14 frames a second, was 32), fading in over its first 15% and out over its last 30%, 0.19 studs at most (was 0.32), so the flame reads as one small steady flame with a soft pulse, not a blink. The outer prongs (the Tines joint) no longer fade on the owner's screen, so the flames stay on solid points; the aura dims on a match turn by the tier's quiet share like every cue's. The lowest rung of the Halloween cues' effects ladder.",
